This is a derivative work — a Scala 3 / Cats port of Haskell QuickCheck's
`Test.QuickCheck.Monadic` module.

Ported from: QuickCheck (https://github.com/nick8325/quickcheck)
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  Copyright (c) 2000-2019, Koen Claessen
  Copyright (c) 2006-2008, Björn Bringert
  Copyright (c) 2009-2019, Nick Smallbone

The `PropertyM` monad, its runners (`monadic`, `monadicIO`, ...), and combinators
(`run`, `pick`, `pre`, `wp`, `assert`, `stop`, `monitor`, `forAllM`) are translations
of the corresponding QuickCheck definitions, adapted to Scala 3 over the Cats
typeclass hierarchy and cats-effect, with `TestControl`-based runners added.

Built on: ScalaCheck (https://github.com/typelevel/scalacheck)
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  Copyright (c) 2007-2021, Rickard Nilsson

The code lives in the `org.scalacheck` package because it depends on ScalaCheck
internals (`Gen.gen`, `Gen.R#doApply/retrieve/withLabels`, `gen.Unsafe.promote`,
`Prop.startSeed`). ScalaCheck is a dependency, not vendored here.
